<Project>
  <!--
    The one build file the fork adds.

    Why it exists at all. SCRIPT TOOL MODE needs a Lua interpreter, and the dependency can't be
    taken the standard way: Content.Server.csproj is an upstream file, and the fork's rule forbids
    changing upstream (the one exception being the ai_data/ line in the root .gitignore).

    Why this works and touches nothing else. There is no root Directory.Build.props in the tree,
    and MSBuild takes the FIRST one found walking up from the project directory
    (Microsoft.Common.props, GetDirectoryNameOfFileAbove). That means this file is visible only to
    Content.Server: RobustToolbox stops at its own RobustToolbox/Directory.Build.props, the other
    Content.* projects sit above it and don't see it, and there's nothing for us to override —
    there would be something to override only if a root one existed.

    Why two lines, not one. Central Package Management is enabled in this tree
    (RobustToolbox/MSBuild/Robust.Properties.targets: ManagePackageVersionsCentrally=true), so a
    PackageReference must go without a Version, with the version coming from PackageVersion. The
    root Directory.Packages.props is upstream and must not be touched; items from both files are
    merged, so we declare our own PackageVersion here.

    WHAT MUST NOT BE DONE HERE: creating Content.Server/Directory.Packages.props. By the same
    "first one walking up the tree" rule, it would override the root one entirely and wipe out the
    versions of every other package.

    Why MoonSharp is safe specifically in Content.Server: the runtime sandbox is disabled on the
    server (ServerOptions.Sandboxing = false), and AssemblyTypeChecker is only run against
    Content.Client and Content.Shared (Content.IntegrationTests/Tests/Utility/SandboxTest.cs). This
    package must never be pulled into Content.Shared under any circumstances — it lives on
    reflection.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageVersion Include="MoonSharp" Version="2.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="MoonSharp" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
